Feature: slice-2 / landing-page
Branch: feat/web-app-slice-2
Verified: 2026-05-28
Anchored to: docs/18 §8.1 (Landing page composition)

What was built
==============
Replaced the scaffold placeholder home with a full marketing landing,
composed of six reusable sections. All copy routes through next-intl
(messages/{pl,en}.json) — zero hard-coded strings.

New components (marketing-site/src/components/marketing/):
- Navbar.tsx — sticky top, brand mark + Cennik link + LocaleSwitcher
  + Log-in (cross-origin to app.superwizor.ai per §5 R3) + Ember
  "Zarejestruj się" CTA.
- LocaleSwitcher.tsx — two-button PL/EN toggle preserving the current
  path. Uses usePathname() + routing.locales; aware of the as-needed
  routing convention.
- Hero.tsx — overline + display heading with Ember accent + serif
  subhead + primary/secondary CTA. Secondary CTA scrolls to
  HowItWorks section via #how anchor.
- HowItWorks.tsx — three numbered cards (01/02/03) describing
  Record → AI processes → Get report. Roboto-Mono tags match the
  label treatment used elsewhere.
- Features.tsx — six-card 1/2/3 responsive grid: transcript, report,
  supervision pointers, RODO, org mode, platform support.
- Audience.tsx — three glass cards (gradient + glass-border) for
  Therapists / Supervisors / Clinics. Aurora-coloured overline so the
  section reads as distinct rhythm vs. Features.
- CtaBand.tsx — full-width band with Ember→Aurora gradient pulling
  the user to "Try 3 free sessions". Primary + secondary CTAs.
- Footer.tsx — three-column nav (Product / Legal / Company) +
  brand mark + tagline + copyright + "Made in Poland" mark.

Modified:
- src/app/[locale]/page.tsx — composition wires all 7 sections.
- messages/pl.json + en.json — extended from feature 2's scaffold
  to ~25 KB each: hero, how.steps.{record,process,report},
  features.items.{6 keys}, audience.items.{3 keys}, cta, footer,
  nav extensions.

How verified
============
1. `pnpm build` exit 0 — both /pl and /en pre-render statically.
   No new deprecation warnings, no TypeScript errors. Build output
   captured implicitly in the dev-server start that followed.

2. Live render at http://localhost:3000/ (Preview MCP):
   - home-pl-{mobile,tablet,desktop}.png — 375x812, 768x1024,
     1280x800 viewport-clipped views of the hero region.
   - home-en-{mobile,tablet,desktop}.png — same dimensions, EN
     locale.
   - home-pl-full.png and home-en-full.png — fullPage screenshots
     (1280 wide, document-height). These prove ALL six sections
     compose correctly top-to-bottom: nav → hero → how → features
     → audience → CTA band → footer.
   - scripts/snap-full.mjs added to the project for full-page
     captures going forward.

3. Visual confirmation (every PNG opened with Read):
   - PL desktop hero: "Drugi mózg superwizora." with Ember accent,
     Polish overline "POLSKI CO-PILOT DLA PSYCHOTERAPEUTÓW",
     subhead about RODO, two CTAs.
   - EN desktop full: hero + "Three steps from session to report"
     + "Everything a supervisor needs" + "Private practice,
     clinics, supervisors" + "Try 3 free sessions" + footer with
     Product/Legal/Company columns. All English.
   - PL full: same composition, Polish copy throughout. Diacritics
     (ż, ó, ę, ą, ć, ł) render cleanly via Montserrat latin-ext
     subset.
   - Mobile (375): nav collapses (Pricing + Login hidden behind
     `hidden sm:inline`); hero stacks; CTAs full-width; sections
     stack vertically.

4. LocaleSwitcher: visible top-right in nav. PL chip Ember-filled
   when locale=pl; EN chip Ember-filled when locale=en. Hrefs
   point at the same path under the other locale (as-needed).

5. preview_console_logs (error) returns "No console logs" — no
   client-side errors after the rebuild.

Compliance with docs/18
=======================
- ✓ §8.1: "Copy describing what Superwizor is, screenshots, CTA →
  register" — copy ✓, CTAs ✓, screenshots deferred (placeholder
  images can land alongside Slice 3 or marketing assets).
- ✓ §5 R3: Log-in is `<a href="https://app.superwizor.ai/login">`
  — no Firebase login flow on superwizor.ai origin.
- ✓ §14.5: no hard-coded UI strings; every label/heading routes
  through messages/*.json.
- ✓ §14.4: hreflang alternates still emitted by the layout (the
  layout from feature 2 is unchanged on this axis).

Known gaps (deferred to subsequent features)
============================================
- Pricing page is wired in nav but its actual content lives in
  feature 6 (`pricing-page`). /pricing currently 404s.
- /register/therapist linked by Hero + Navbar + CtaBand — Slice 3
  builds those forms.
- /legal/{terms,privacy,dpa} linked by Footer — feature 7
  (`legal-static-pages`) backfills.
- Product screenshots / illustration art — placeholder text
  describes what the screenshots would show; actual images can be
  added without code churn (the Features/HowItWorks cards have
  unused space ready).
- AuthStatusBadge (feature 4) still visible in dev — flagged but
  doesn't ship in production builds.

